#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# exception_data

#% text
# `exception_data(exc)` gives the data association of the exception `exc`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `exception(type)` has an empty association; data that is not an association is under the key `payload`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
exception_data(exception(data_error, assoc(data -> 42)))
#% output
#= assoc(data -> 42)

#% cell
exception_data(exception(invalid_expression, a + b))
#% output
#= assoc(payload -> a + b)

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# Data that is a list or a string is kept under `payload`; the argument must be an exception:

#% cell
[exception_data(exception(t1, [1, 2])), exception_data(exception(t1, "text")), exception_data(5)]
#% output
#= [assoc(payload -> [1, 2]), assoc(payload -> "text"), failure(no_match, exception_data, [5])]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `exception`, `exception_type`
